For UVa 10082 **"WERTYU"**, the task is to replace every character with the key immediately to its left on a standard keyboard.

A simple student-style C solution:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main()
{
    char keyboard[] = "`1234567890-=QWERTYUIOP[]\\ASDFGHJKL;'ZXCVBNM,./";
    char line[1000];

    while(fgets(line, sizeof(line), stdin))
    {
        for(int i = 0; line[i] != '\0'; i++)
        {
            if(line[i] == ' ')
            {
                printf(" ");
                continue;
            }

            for(int j = 0; keyboard[j] != '\0'; j++)
            {
                if(line[i] == keyboard[j])
                {
                    printf("%c", keyboard[j - 1]);
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return 0;
}
```

### Sample Input

```text
O S, GOMR YPFSU/
```

### Sample Output

```text
I AM FINE TODAY.
```

### Idea

* Store the keyboard layout in a string.
* For each input character:

  * If it's a space, print a space.
  * Otherwise, find it in the keyboard string and print the character just before it.

This is a very common beginner-friendly UVa solution and looks naturally student-written.
